A||||10||Cheever3000||Lights on calipers - seen on an import ||||6||
Z||000000||Cheever3000||10-17-2001||02:56 PM||||The flashy stuff never appealed to me much, but last night I saw a shiny black import with 2 little red lights on each brake caliper.  And I liked it.  The car was not riced out in any other way, just plain, except for those lights.  At first I thought, oh it's those valve stem lights, but they didn't turn with the wheels, they just kind of twinkled from behind as the wheels turned. <BR>||||reg||6
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||10-17-2001||03:47 PM||||what would be really cool, is orange neons, hidden from view... put them on really dim, and people would think your brakes are glowing.. hehe.. maybe put a sparker in there too?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>(am I kidding? even I'm not sure anymore....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||12
Z||000002||fierospeeder||10-17-2001||03:55 PM||||jc whitney is selling  flashing light, or light for your valve stem caps on your tires.<P>pull off your valve stem cap, and screw the light on.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fformula88||10-17-2001||04:25 PM||||I saw a car the other day (an import, maybe not a Honda not sure cuz it was night and behind me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)  It had small red lights sticking out of the hood where the windshield squirts would normally be!  Sorry, but that looked plain stupid!  Like it was a frog with eyes on the top of its head!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Nashco||10-17-2001||05:45 PM||||Yeah, I've seen the squirter lights and the valve stem lights....they look so dopey!  I could see lighting the brakes (as cheever saw) if you had some sweet brembos with red and machined aluminum finish, but that would only be cool at a stand still.  What's the point...I just don't get it?  How much attention could a person be starving for?  What's next, fog lights on the SIDE of the car?<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000005||Philphine||10-17-2001||05:48 PM||||you can get those washer lights at auto zone. just saw them this weekend. i had some marker lights behind my wheels a long time ago. thought it was kind of neat but since i wanted them to just shine through the wheel and not under the car i think i had them on the unsprung part of the suspension and they pretty much rattled to death.<P>now on my '87 and my chevy i have 3m red reflective tape that runs around the wheel behind the spokes. sounds tacky but it's really nice since it's behind the spokes. did it about 3 years ago and no pealing and still very reflective. all comments positive. i want to do my gt too but i want to use black tape (reflects silver), it's harder to find.<p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 10-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fformula88||10-17-2001||08:00 PM||||Nice brembo brakes reminded me of how people will paint their calipers to show them off from behind the wheels.  I have no problem with that... although the brembo's would look better.  What kills me is when they paint their rear drums a shiney red or yellow!  I just think it looks silly.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||sqoach||10-17-2001||10:21 PM||||There's a dodge avenger in town that has those lights on the windshield squirters. And they're purple! He also has chrome hub-caps...lmao!<P>Also, there's a guy with an 88(?) grand am. The paint looks like crap. A bunch is chipping off the hood. He has neons under his car, and strobe light things in front. And some other lights that just stay on in front (no, not the headlights silly)<BR>Anyway, I just have this face  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> when I see it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cheever3000||10-17-2001||10:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR> there's a guy with an 88(?) grand am. The paint looks like crap. A bunch is chipping off the hood. <HR></BLOCKQUOTE>He obviously doesn't know he can get the dealership to repaint it for free.  There were a couple of years when they had a bad batch of paint.  I know, cuz my 89 G.A. had the same problem.  Sure was glad somebody told me it could be fixed!<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Nashco||10-18-2001||09:29 AM||||I heard about some cool caliper lights on a champ car in the Portland race, on a Toyota...anybody know anything about this?<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000010||rogergarrison||10-18-2001||01:47 PM||||Ive done lots of those. 84-89 GMs. They only did it if it had the original paint, and you were the original owner. As far as I know, the program is finished now since all those cars are now 15 years old and not even worth the cost of the paint job. It was mostly on GrandAms, Cavaliers, Celebrities.||||reg||1
